# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
import Vue from "vue";
import * as VueNamespace from "vue";
import { config } from "vue";

Vue.config.keyCodes = { f1: 112 };
VueNamespace.config.keyCodes = { f1: 112 };
config.keyCodes = { f1: 112 };

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-import.js:6:1 lint/nursery/noVueDeprecatedConfigKeyCodes ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i The Vue.config.keyCodes option is deprecated and has no effect in Vue 3.
  
    4 │ import { config } from "vue";
    5 │ 
  > 6 │ Vue.config.keyCodes = { f1: 112 };
      │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    7 │ VueNamespace.config.keyCodes = { f1: 112 };
    8 │ config.keyCodes = { f1: 112 };
  
  i Vue 3 no longer supports custom key names, because they rely on the deprecated KeyboardEvent.keyCode browser property.
  
  i Remove this option, and use the key name in kebab-case as the modifier instead, such as @keyup.page-down. See the Vue 3 migration guide for more information.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

